00:05:11.032 --> 00:05:12.633
Another little-known fact

00:05:12.633 --> 00:05:14.902
: when my family

00:05:14.902 --> 00:05:15.970
or my dad makes tea,

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.672
he often opens a whole

00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:19.207
can of Wansui brand nuts,

00:05:19.207 --> 00:05:21.075
scatters them on the table, and eats them while making tea.

00:05:21.075 --> 00:05:22.543
Do you know where macadamia nuts

00:05:22.543 --> 00:05:24.112
originated?

00:05:24.112 --> 00:05:24.912
No,

00:05:24.912 --> 00:05:25.680
it's from South Africa.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.814
The

00:05:26.814 --> 00:05:29.016
reason they're called macadamia nuts is because

00:05:29.016 --> 00:05:30.601
they're

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:31.836
commercially grown in Hawaii

00:05:31.853 --> 00:05:33.254
, but

00:05:33.254 --> 00:05:35.723
their original birthplace is South Africa.

00:05:35.723 --> 00:05:37.325
They should be officially called

00:05:37.325 --> 00:05:38.025
South African nuts.

00:05:38.025 --> 00:05:39.927
We need to officially recognize them as

00:05:39.927 --> 00:05:41.229
South African nuts. And cashews?

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:42.797
Do you know where cashews are?

00:05:42.797 --> 00:05:44.298
They're from Brazil

00:05:44.298 --> 00:05:45.433
. These cashews

00:05:45.433 --> 00:05:46.734
I'm showing you

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.569
are from Brazil, born and raised there.

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:49.804
But this batch of cashews

00:05:49.804 --> 00:05:51.005
isn't from Brazil either.

00:05:51.005 --> 00:05:52.874
Now, most cashews

00:05:52.874 --> 00:05:55.777
come from Southeast Asia, Ivory Coast, and India. They fly directly to the production

00:05:55.777 --> 00:05:56.611
areas

00:05:56.611 --> 00:05:59.247
to personally inspect

00:05:59.247 --> 00:06:00.882
and obtain the raw materials before

00:06:00.882 --> 00:06:02.650
shipping them back to Taiwan. Now

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.485
, do you know where these almonds

00:06:04.485 --> 00:06:05.887
came from?

00:06:07.121 --> 00:06:08.389
California, USA.

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:09.791
Don't think I'm having an easy time; I

00:06:09.791 --> 00:06:11.259
started the machine in just a few minutes

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:12.627
and I can't even speak anymore.

00:06:12.627 --> 00:06:14.779
California

00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:16.514
has a lot of almonds besides peaches. Of course,

00:06:16.514 --> 00:06:18.115
you can't just give

00:06:18.115 --> 00:06:19.450
something to someone to eat right after you buy it

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.519
. Actually, it goes through many steps.

00:06:21.519 --> 00:06:22.954
Now, let's go inside

00:06:22.954 --> 00:06:24.322
. Yes, as

00:06:24.322 --> 00:06:25.857
you can see above

00:06:25.857 --> 00:06:27.325
before we go in,

00:06:27.325 --> 00:06:28.125
it's a noisy place,

00:06:28.125 --> 00:06:29.794
so you must wear soundproof protective gear

00:06:29.794 --> 00:06:31.195
to enter . So, the following video

00:06:31.195 --> 00:06:32.430
will be narrated.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.164
Anyway, I'm wearing a mask,

00:06:33.164 --> 00:06:34.599
so you can't see what I'm saying.

00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:36.334
Nuts are agricultural products,

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:38.135
and each batch has some differences.

00:06:38.135 --> 00:06:40.371
As long as the moisture content is different from the standard value,

00:06:40.371 --> 00:06:42.106
the roasting parameters need to be adjusted.

00:06:42.106 --> 00:06:44.575
So, when you're manufacturing food machinery,

00:06:44.575 --> 00:06:47.011
you can imagine that

00:06:47.011 --> 00:06:48.946
if the angle of this feeding machine is flatter today,

00:06:48.946 --> 00:06:51.315
it will fall naturally according to gravity and

00:06:51.315 --> 00:06:53.217
be able to catch... The amount that can be collected will be more

00:06:53.217 --> 00:06:55.319
. If its angle is tilted slightly,

00:06:55.319 --> 00:06:57.188
the amount it can collect will be less.

00:06:57.188 --> 00:06:58.856
Why is it important to control this amount

00:06:58.856 --> 00:07:00.525
? Because when it goes into the roasting process,

00:07:00.525 --> 00:07:02.760
you can see the final product.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.728
You can observe this section

00:07:03.728 --> 00:07:05.396
and see that the average thickness of this section

00:07:05.396 --> 00:07:06.497
is actually the same.

00:07:06.497 --> 00:07:08.799
Why does this horizontal thickness need to be the same?

00:07:08.799 --> 00:07:10.401
Because if some of the filling is

00:07:10.401 --> 00:07:11.936
too thin,

00:07:11.936 --> 00:07:13.938
it will be drier after roasting

00:07:13.938 --> 00:07:15.406
. If it is too thick,

00:07:15.406 --> 00:07:17.041
the middle will not be roasted nicely enough.

00:07:17.041 --> 00:07:19.210
So the purpose of roasting with an average thickness

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.411
is to ensure that

00:07:20.411 --> 00:07:22.013
the degree of roasting and quality of the nuts

00:07:22.013 --> 00:07:24.382
delivered to each convenience store

00:07:24.382 --> 00:07:26.050
is consistent . After it falls here,

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.386
it is leveled by vibration and shaking.

00:07:28.386 --> 00:07:30.021
After leveling, you will see a

00:07:30.021 --> 00:07:32.523
near-infrared analyzer and a colorimeter.

00:07:32.523 --> 00:07:34.759
It can monitor in real time whether

00:07:34.759 --> 00:07:37.762
the moisture content and roasting color of each product

00:07:37.762 --> 00:07:38.696
are the same.

00:07:38.696 --> 00:07:40.298
Because it used to be done manually,

00:07:40.298 --> 00:07:41.165
you can imagine what would happen

00:07:41.165 --> 00:07:42.934
if the experienced chef... If your eyesight isn't good and

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:44.602
you're not getting enough lutein,

00:07:44.602 --> 00:07:46.837
the color of the nuts will look different.

00:07:46.837 --> 00:07:48.940
Look at these two – before

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.708
and after roasting. The unroasted ones

00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:52.843
look like this. After peeling, the inside is white.

00:07:52.843 --> 00:07:54.211
After roasting,

00:07:54.211 --> 00:07:55.212
the

00:07:55.212 --> 00:07:57.949
inside has a dark coffee or light coffee color;

00:07:57.949 --> 00:07:59.917
that's roasted almonds.

00:07:59.917 --> 00:08:01.352
Of course, besides looking different,

00:08:01.352 --> 00:08:02.954
the taste and

00:08:02.954 --> 00:08:04.906
aroma are completely different too.

00:08:04.906 --> 00:08:07.508
Next, they go into the laser sorting machine

00:08:07.508 --> 00:08:09.243
. This laser sorting machine

00:08:09.243 --> 00:08:10.578
doesn't require manual selection; it

00:08:10.578 --> 00:08:13.514
uses two lasers and halogen lamps for dual inspection.

00:08:13.514 --> 00:08:16.617
It monitors thousands of fallen nuts every minute.

00:08:16.617 --> 00:08:19.053
If the computer determines that the shape isn't good,

00:08:19.053 --> 00:08:20.254
the color is dull,

00:08:20.254 --> 00:08:22.290
or there's a small hole from an insect bite,

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.725
it will spray high-pressure air

00:08:24.725 --> 00:08:26.360
within fractions of a second of the nut falling

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.362
and blow the bad nut away.

00:08:28.362 --> 00:08:30.097
It's knocked out from there.

00:08:30.097 --> 00:08:31.799
And did you see that button above?

00:08:31.799 --> 00:08:32.533
(Just kidding.) Press it.

00:08:32.533 --> 00:08:33.701
(Just kidding.) When the entire factory is shut

00:08:33.701 --> 00:08:35.469
down, the nuts pass through this conveyor belt

00:08:35.469 --> 00:08:37.305
and travel all the way here.

00:08:37.305 --> 00:08:38.706
So,

00:08:38.706 --> 00:08:40.875
as you can see, these are insect-damaged or broken

00:08:40.875 --> 00:08:42.777
, but some good ones are blown off –

00:08:42.777 --> 00:08:44.545
this is the loss we have to bear

00:08:44.545 --> 00:08:46.347
. These qualified almonds

00:08:46.347 --> 00:08:47.715
will be sorted in batches

00:08:47.715 --> 00:08:49.750
and sent back to this conveyor belt

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.285
, then into these two rollers.

00:08:51.285 --> 00:08:53.754
These rollers are for spraying oil.

00:08:53.754 --> 00:08:55.890
Because some of their components have flavor,

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.792
they can be seasoned simultaneously

00:08:57.792 --> 00:08:58.659
. After seasoning,

00:08:58.659 --> 00:09:01.228
when you buy small packages of nuts

00:09:01.228 --> 00:09:02.897
at 7-Eleven or FamilyMart, the nuts

00:09:02.897 --> 00:09:04.799
aren't picked out one by one; instead

00:09:04.799 --> 00:09:06.600
, they're categorized using

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.168
a

00:09:07.168 --> 00:09:08.502
petal-shaped measuring machine.

00:09:08.502 --> 00:09:11.105
Each petal-shaped measuring machine is like a pipeline.

00:09:11.105 --> 00:09:14.342
During production, the material cups collect material from each measuring machine,

00:09:14.342 --> 00:09:15.810
ensuring that

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:17.945
each package contains all the mixed nuts.

00:09:17.945 --> 00:09:19.947
This petal-shaped measuring machine

00:09:19.947 --> 00:09:21.749
has many independent scales

00:09:21.749 --> 00:09:22.416
, unlike

00:09:22.416 --> 00:09:24.185
simply grabbing a handful and mixing them together

00:09:24.185 --> 00:09:26.320
. Instead, the computer instantly arranges and combines them

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.888
, summing them up to

00:09:27.888 --> 00:09:29.924
the exact weight required for one pipeline.

00:09:29.924 --> 00:09:30.891
This method is very clever.

00:09:30.891 --> 00:09:32.793
For example, if I want to produce a product,

00:09:32.793 --> 00:09:34.795
I can divide the raw materials into four mixing stages

00:09:34.795 --> 00:09:36.897
and then slowly convey them along the track,

00:09:36.897 --> 00:09:40.434
ensuring the most even distribution. After distributing the mixed nuts into each package,

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:41.836
an oxygen absorber is added

00:09:41.836 --> 00:09:43.070
before they enter the packaging

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:45.239
. It cuts the nuts inside

00:09:45.239 --> 00:09:47.508
and then places them into individual packets

00:09:47.508 --> 00:09:49.677
. So, what if one day you eat a food item

00:09:49.677 --> 00:09:51.312
and find two oxygen absorbers?

00:09:51.312 --> 00:09:52.146
No problem,

00:09:52.146 --> 00:09:53.314
you're lucky!

00:09:53.314 --> 00:09:53.814
Remember,

00:09:53.814 --> 00:09:54.949
each time you open the package, you

00:09:54.949 --> 00:09:56.117
can discard the oxygen absorber

00:09:56.117 --> 00:09:57.785
, but don't discard the desiccant.

00:09:57.785 --> 00:10:00.221
After adding the oxygen absorber, it's conveyed in

00:10:00.221 --> 00:10:01.422
and falls down

00:10:01.422 --> 00:10:03.024
to the food packaging.

00:10:03.024 --> 00:10:03.691
So you see,

00:10:03.691 --> 00:10:04.959
the principles of machinery

00:10:04.959 --> 00:10:06.961
aren't just applicable to industrial production.

00:10:06.961 --> 00:10:08.662
In food processing,

00:10:08.662 --> 00:10:11.198
if you understand the workings of many machines

00:10:11.198 --> 00:10:12.666
and the principles of many production lines,

00:10:12.666 --> 00:10:13.467
you'll find

00:10:13.467 --> 00:10:15.736
the world of industrial manufacturing very interesting.

00:10:15.736 --> 00:10:16.904
With good ideas, you

00:10:16.904 --> 00:10:18.472
have endless possibilities.

00:10:18.472 --> 00:10:19.640
What you see now

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.575
are freshly packaged nuts

00:10:21.575 --> 00:10:24.211
that fall through a metal detector

00:10:24.211 --> 00:10:25.646
into the packaging.

00:10:25.646 --> 00:10:26.814
Before the final sealing,

00:10:26.814 --> 00:10:28.449
there's a crucial step:

00:10:28.449 --> 00:10:30.151
filling and deoxygenating

00:10:30.151 --> 00:10:31.952
the packaging before it can be sealed.

00:10:31.952 --> 00:10:34.989
Why do factories go through this trouble?

00:10:34.989 --> 00:10:37.591
Because once you open the packaging and expose it to oxygen,

00:10:37.591 --> 00:10:39.960
the chemical chain reaction of oil oxidation

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.196
starts, and its timer begins.

00:10:42.196 --> 00:10:44.065
Gas is injected one second before sealing

00:10:44.065 --> 00:10:45.966
to force out oxygen.

00:10:45.966 --> 00:10:47.835
The lower the oxygen content inside

00:10:47.835 --> 00:10:49.937
, the less likely the nuts are to oxidize.

00:10:49.937 --> 00:10:51.939
That's why they

00:10:51.939 --> 00:10:54.842
taste just like they were fresh from the factory even after six months .

00:10:54.842 --> 00:10:55.776
Also, let me show you

00:10:55.776 --> 00:10:57.578
a 7-Eleven limited edition.

00:10:57.578 --> 00:10:59.713
Have you ever seen these small

00:10:59.713 --> 00:11:02.216
packages in convenience stores? The packaging is really cool!

00:11:02.216 --> 00:11:03.184
It's like this:

00:11:03.184 --> 00:11:04.018
bundles

00:11:04.018 --> 00:11:05.719
rise up, and then

00:11:05.719 --> 00:11:08.389
there's something like a baller in the middle

00:11:08.389 --> 00:11:10.191
that turns the package into a cylindrical shape.

00:11:10.191 --> 00:11:11.926
Then,

00:11:11.926 --> 00:11:13.961
the food inside is fed in

00:11:13.961 --> 00:11:15.429
and rolled. After that,

00:11:15.429 --> 00:11:17.865
there's a closing and pulling action at the bottom.

00:11:17.865 --> 00:11:19.500
The pulling action is very important.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.035
First, it squeezes the package to make it

00:11:21.035 --> 00:11:22.570
slightly bulging

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.839
. Second, it can cut it at the same time,

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:25.706
so it becomes

00:11:25.706 --> 00:11:26.740
a 7-Eleven... After you buy

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.176
the packaged food that you can tear open and eat directly

00:11:29.176 --> 00:11:30.845
, even though it has already undergone

00:11:30.845 --> 00:11:32.413
so many tests and measurements

00:11:32.413 --> 00:11:34.315
, before it is finally delivered to the consumer,

00:11:34.315 --> 00:11:35.716
they will use a weighing machine

00:11:35.716 --> 00:11:38.152
to calculate the weight of each product before shipment

00:11:38.152 --> 00:11:39.753
and check for any suspicious figures.

00:11:39.753 --> 00:11:41.856
If it is not within the standard range,

00:11:41.856 --> 00:11:43.190
it will be rejected.

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.758
Of course, in addition to small packages,

00:11:44.758 --> 00:11:47.261
you can also see canned and large canned products

00:11:47.261 --> 00:11:49.196
in Carrefour, PX Mart, or hypermarkets

00:11:49.196 --> 00:11:50.931
using different packaging methods.

00:11:50.931 --> 00:11:52.566
Even the folding of the cardboard boxes.

00:11:52.566 --> 00:11:53.334
In the past,

00:11:53.334 --> 00:11:55.069
when doing this kind of packaging,

00:11:55.069 --> 00:11:56.237
22 people

00:11:56.237 --> 00:11:57.671
could only pack about

00:11:57.671 --> 00:11:58.572
500 boxes

00:11:58.572 --> 00:12:00.274
a day . But now,

00:12:00.274 --> 00:12:01.475
after switching to automation and using robotic arms,

00:12:01.475 --> 00:12:02.977
4 to 6 people

00:12:02.977 --> 00:12:04.411
can pack

00:12:04.411 --> 00:12:05.479
1,500 boxes a day

00:12:05.479 --> 00:12:06.580
, which saves a lot of

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.383
repetitive and labor-intensive tasks.

00:12:09.383 --> 00:12:10.985
So you will see later.

00:12:10.985 --> 00:12:13.487
Finally,

00:12:13.487 --> 00:12:14.788
the Kawasaki arm

00:12:14.788 --> 00:12:16.123
will pack and package it for you on the entire pallet.

00:12:16.123 --> 00:12:16.724
And did you know that

00:12:16.724 --> 00:12:18.159
even screwing on and locking the lid

00:12:18.159 --> 00:12:20.461
was still done manually until last year to check

00:12:20.461 --> 00:12:22.429
the quality of the lock? Not good,

00:12:22.429 --> 00:12:24.098
but now because of the iteration and automation

00:12:24.098 --> 00:12:25.900
, robotic arms help with moving and transferring,

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.168
which can

00:12:27.168 --> 00:12:29.870
effectively reduce the burden on employees in the factory management.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.505
Good. From the previous exit

00:12:31.505 --> 00:12:32.606
to the current entrance,

00:12:32.606 --> 00:12:33.958
you can see that there is a

00:12:33.958 --> 00:12:34.742
copper wall here

00:12:34.742 --> 00:12:36.143
, which is to wrap it up

00:12:36.143 --> 00:12:39.180
and separate the items that will come into contact with food

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.281
in one area.

00:12:40.281 --> 00:12:41.849
And now the packaging is out.

00:12:41.849 --> 00:12:44.084
You can get this packaging at 7-Eleven.

00:12:44.084 --> 00:12:44.852
This is another area

00:12:44.852 --> 00:12:47.021
, so everyone's clothing will be lighter.

00:12:47.021 --> 00:12:47.521
And many

00:12:47.521 --> 00:12:48.956
factories,

00:12:48.956 --> 00:12:50.224
whether they are shoe factories

00:12:50.224 --> 00:12:51.525
, bicycle factories

00:12:51.525 --> 00:12:53.627
, or parts factories like the ones we have filmed before,

00:12:53.627 --> 00:12:54.662
will have a standard area

00:12:54.662 --> 00:12:55.663
that looks

00:12:55.663 --> 00:12:56.830
like this.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.933
It shows the standard for today ,

00:12:58.933 --> 00:13:00.768
and it will look like this

00:13:00.768 --> 00:13:02.636
until the last pack is

00:13:02.636 --> 00:13:03.604
finished

00:13:03.604 --> 00:13:05.372
tonight.

00:13:05.372 --> 00:13:06.907
Another interesting thing

00:13:06.907 --> 00:13:07.942
is that you see it every day

00:13:07.942 --> 00:13:09.410
, but you have probably never used it.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.412
There

00:13:11.412 --> 00:13:12.947
is a QR code here. The barcode

00:13:12.947 --> 00:13:14.281
isn't for making friends

00:13:14.281 --> 00:13:15.649
or paying money.

00:13:15.649 --> 00:13:16.383
When

00:13:16.383 --> 00:13:18.252
you scan it with your phone,

00:13:18.252 --> 00:13:20.654
it reveals the product's entire origin and traceability.

00:13:20.654 --> 00:13:21.622
You can

00:13:21.622 --> 00:13:23.190
see which country it came from

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.426
, various microbiological inspection reports

00:13:25.426 --> 00:13:27.294
, and that they inspect each batch individually.

00:13:27.294 --> 00:13:28.796
It even shows

00:13:28.796 --> 00:13:29.930
the origin of

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.165
each individual

00:13:31.165 --> 00:13:32.166
seasoning ingredient.

00:13:32.166 --> 00:13:32.933
With this

00:13:32.933 --> 00:13:33.801
traceability,

00:13:33.801 --> 00:13:35.002
if a

00:13:35.002 --> 00:13:35.736
problem arises,

00:13:35.736 --> 00:13:37.204
the factory can trace it

00:13:37.204 --> 00:13:39.173
back to where the issue occurred.

00:13:39.173 --> 00:13:41.725
Every workstation scans the barcode, and the

00:13:41.725 --> 00:13:43.360
information is recorded in the system,

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.162
allowing you to find the problem.

00:13:45.162 --> 00:13:46.397
So, when you buy a package

00:13:46.397 --> 00:13:47.331
at a convenience store

00:13:47.331 --> 00:13:48.399
or supermarket

00:13:48.399 --> 00:13:49.533
, it has undergone

00:13:49.533 --> 00:13:50.935
so many complex

00:13:50.935 --> 00:13:52.069
checks

00:13:52.069 --> 00:13:53.370
and so many machines

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:54.738
before finally reaching you

00:13:54.738 --> 00:13:56.206
, giving you peace of mind.

00:13:56.206 --> 00:13:57.074
I have a child, and

00:13:57.074 --> 00:13:58.042
you put things in your mouth

00:13:58.042 --> 00:13:59.209
. If there are any strange

00:13:59.209 --> 00:14:00.311
or unseen microorganisms

00:14:00.311 --> 00:14:01.445
in the production line,

00:14:01.445 --> 00:14:02.846
it would be very bad.

00:14:02.846 --> 00:14:04.048
That's why I often tell everyone

00:14:04.048 --> 00:14:05.082
not to buy

00:14:05.082 --> 00:14:06.517
those live-streamed products.

00:14:06.517 --> 00:14:07.685
I believe

00:14:07.685 --> 00:14:09.920
there aren't any such things behind them.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.089
Because when the government was promoting product traceability,

00:14:12.089 --> 00:14:13.290
they found many manufacturers

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.426
to work together on product traceability,

00:14:15.426 --> 00:14:17.294
but only this one passed.

00:14:17.294 --> 00:14:18.429
No wonder Janet said,

00:14:18.429 --> 00:14:19.530
"This isn't Wansui brand

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:20.798
, I won't eat it."

00:14:20.798 --> 00:14:21.832
Janet

00:14:21.832 --> 00:14:23.233
is afraid of getting a stomachache.

00:14:23.233 --> 00:14:24.034
So, to this day, they

00:14:24.034 --> 00:14:25.469
have a market share of about 70%

00:14:25.469 --> 00:14:26.737
in Taiwan.

00:14:26.737 --> 00:14:27.871
Next,

00:14:27.871 --> 00:14:29.039
we're going to a place

00:14:29.039 --> 00:14:31.308
