00:22:42.866 --> 00:22:45.101
So you have to go to the laboratory.

00:22:45.101 --> 00:22:47.804
Since we're already at the food factory,

00:22:47.804 --> 00:22:49.539
I'm sure everyone is familiar with

00:22:49.539 --> 00:22:51.374
the expiration date.

00:22:51.374 --> 00:22:52.509
There are many

00:22:52.509 --> 00:22:53.643
rumors about

00:22:53.643 --> 00:22:55.545
whether you can still eat it

00:22:55.545 --> 00:22:56.513
after the expiration date.

00:22:56.513 --> 00:22:58.482
Although many foods are

00:22:58.482 --> 00:22:59.583
tested for aflatoxin

00:22:59.583 --> 00:23:01.284
in laboratories

00:23:01.284 --> 00:23:03.353
before leaving the factory, and although

00:23:03.353 --> 00:23:05.856
there's still an expiration date on the food

00:23:05.856 --> 00:23:08.458
, when we asked the manufacturer,

00:23:08.458 --> 00:23:09.526
they told us that

00:23:09.526 --> 00:23:12.496
there's something more important than the expiration date

00:23:12.496 --> 00:23:14.998
—your... The storage location of this food

00:23:14.998 --> 00:23:16.399
basically determines its preservation method

00:23:16.399 --> 00:23:17.968
. If possible,

00:23:17.968 --> 00:23:19.302
store it in

00:23:19.302 --> 00:23:20.537
a place away from direct sunlight

00:23:20.537 --> 00:23:22.806
, or in a cool, dark place in a cabinet.

00:23:22.806 --> 00:23:24.274
Only then can you refer to

00:23:24.274 --> 00:23:25.375
its expiration date

00:23:25.375 --> 00:23:27.611
. If you leave it in your car

00:23:27.611 --> 00:23:28.745
, for example, when going on a trip

00:23:28.745 --> 00:23:30.046
, exposed to high temperatures

00:23:30.046 --> 00:23:31.014
and direct

00:23:31.014 --> 00:23:32.015
sunlight

00:23:32.015 --> 00:23:33.517
, or in a

00:23:33.517 --> 00:23:35.252
damp, well-ventilated basement

00:23:35.252 --> 00:23:36.553
, or even

00:23:36.553 --> 00:23:38.955
in your toolbox, it

00:23:38.955 --> 00:23:40.490
can still be dangerous

00:23:40.490 --> 00:23:41.992
due to high temperatures and moisture

00:23:41.992 --> 00:23:43.460
, even if it's

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:44.427
within the expiration date.

00:23:44.427 --> 00:23:46.229
This is because aflatoxin is irreversible

00:23:46.229 --> 00:23:47.330
; its levels will increase

00:23:47.330 --> 00:23:48.265
after exposure

00:23:48.265 --> 00:23:49.966
. Furthermore, it's a Group 1 carcinogen

00:23:49.966 --> 00:23:51.701
. Therefore, although

00:23:51.701 --> 00:23:53.637
the detected levels

00:23:53.637 --> 00:23:55.772
are significantly lower than the national standard

00:23:55.772 --> 00:23:56.706
(PPB) , the levels are

00:23:56.706 --> 00:23:57.607
still very low. Even

00:23:57.607 --> 00:24:00.544
with a sample size of one part per billion, testing is still necessary.

00:24:00.544 --> 00:24:01.645
However, if

00:24:01.645 --> 00:24:04.180
the food isn't stored properly,

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:05.815
it can easily

00:24:05.815 --> 00:24:06.816
become dangerous

00:24:06.816 --> 00:24:08.652
. Sometimes,

00:24:08.652 --> 00:24:10.353
even though you buy the food,

00:24:10.353 --> 00:24:12.389
you don't know where it came from.

00:24:12.389 --> 00:24:13.256
It might have

00:24:13.256 --> 00:24:14.257
been sold to you by a friend

00:24:14.257 --> 00:24:15.792
, or by a

00:24:15.792 --> 00:24:18.161
dishonest middleman

00:24:18.161 --> 00:24:19.129
. They might have

00:24:19.129 --> 00:24:20.730
stored it in a bad place, like

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:22.532
leaving it out in the sun for a long time during

00:24:22.532 --> 00:24:23.600
a school sports meet

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:24.401
, and then taking

00:24:24.401 --> 00:24:26.069
the leftovers back to distribute.

00:24:26.069 --> 00:24:27.537
So, if you open a food container

00:24:27.537 --> 00:24:28.305
and find

00:24:28.305 --> 00:24:29.806
it has a rancid smell

00:24:29.806 --> 00:24:31.775
